===============================================================================
THIRD-PARTY MODELS AND LIBRARIES
===============================================================================

This project downloads pre-trained weights at install time. It does not
redistribute them. Every default component is licensed for commercial use, as
the competition rules require:

  BiRefNet / BiRefNet_lite      MIT             ZhengPeng7/BiRefNet
    Primary segmentation model. Commercial use permitted.

  U2-Net (u2net.onnx)           Apache-2.0      xuebinqin/U-2-Net
    Cross-check model. Weights are re-hosted by the rembg project (MIT); the
    original architecture and checkpoints are Apache-2.0.

  OpenCV                        Apache-2.0
  PyTorch / torchvision         BSD-3-Clause
  transformers, timm, kornia    Apache-2.0
  einops, onnxruntime, FastAPI  MIT
  Pillow                        MIT-CMU
  NumPy                         BSD-3-Clause

OPTIONAL, DISABLED BY DEFAULT
-----------------------------
  MobileSAM weights             Apache-2.0      ChaoningZhang/MobileSAM
  ultralytics (its loader)      AGPL-3.0

    The SAM boundary refiner in app/segmentation/sam_refiner.py is off unless
    AUTOMASK_SAM_REFINE=1 is set. The weights are Apache-2.0, but the loader
    used to run them (ultralytics) is AGPL-3.0, which is usually unacceptable
    inside a closed-source commercial backend. Enable it only if you comply with
    AGPL-3.0, hold an Ultralytics commercial licence, or swap in the upstream
    MobileSAM repository (Apache-2.0). The pipeline is fully functional without
    it.

  CLIP (openai/clip-vit-base-patch32)   MIT
    Zero-shot category detection, off unless AUTOMASK_CLIP=1.

TEST DATA
---------
  data/samples/ is generated procedurally by scripts/make_dataset.py. It
  contains no third-party imagery and carries no licence obligations.

  scripts/fetch_dataset.py can additionally download real photographs from
  Wikimedia Commons. Those files keep their own licences, which the script
  records (with author and source page) in the manifest it writes. Check that
  manifest before using any of them outside of testing.
